# Never translate line endings in this repository.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so git would store these files with LF
# and hand them back with CRLF. That matters here more than usual: the files are
# rewritten wholesale by the pipeline every run, and the publish script decides
# whether to commit by comparing what the tools produced against what is in the
# working copy. If git is quietly rewriting one side, every run looks changed
# even when the ladder has not moved -- and a commit means a tag, and a tag
# means a build and a download for everybody.
#
# Marking them -text keeps both sides byte-identical, so "nothing changed"
# stays detectable.
* -text
